{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening","id":609622,"title":"Sell me on Mage: The Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-31T09:55:07-07:00","id":609622,"title":"Sell me on Mage: The Awakening","content":"Based on another thread, I have some issues with Mage since the 1st ed core, but I do want to see past them. I like some of the concepts and almost all the mechanics, and am looking forward to 2nd ed rules.<br /> <br /> The setting, tough...<br /> <br /> Atlantis and the Pentacle never had any appeal to me. And the Seers seem just like a bunch of lunatics that I can pretty much ignore. Because seriously, they're just nuts. And not even in a dangerous way.<br /> <br /> How those things really play together and with other elements to make this game interesting as a modern drama/horror game based on real life people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:07:22-07:00","id":609662,"title":"","content":"This again.<br /> <br /> Have you read the devblogs at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:08:51-07:00","id":609664,"title":"","content":"Some of them, actualy. The Seers included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:10:15-07:00","id":609665,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Op, ninja'd and evidently neither news nor helpful. ^_^o Ah well. Might as well post anyway.<br /> <br /> I don't have the level of understanding of Mage necessary to help, but may be able to point you in the right direction. Dave's made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/437565-second-edition-development-blogs\">a lot of blog posts</a> discussing and teasing 2e, and it's certainly what got me looking at Mage.<br /> <br /> Among these are the current drafts for the Pentacle and Seer write-ups. I've heard that all of those groups became much more vibrant in their focused supplements, and the 2e introductions to them have tried to draw more from those than the 1e core's depictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:12:18-07:00","id":609667,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's not for you. I don't really care for Werewolf the Apocalypse personally though I can definitely see there's lots of well written stuff in it. If you've read the core book and you just don't like it, I'm not seeing what help you're expecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:59:13-07:00","id":609752,"title":"","content":"First, a comment from the developer about Atlantis: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-fate-of-atlantis-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-fate-of-a...the-awakening/</a><br /> <br /> Before I get to your problems I'll go with the sell. You specifically asked how the Pentacle and the Seers can work together to make a modern drama/horror game? Well, did you like the Matrix and the world it posited? Because you have all those elements: A secret, world spanning, conspiracy that controls not just the government, but everyone's fundamental understanding of reality as it is. A conspiracy that is not content to rule people's wallets and homes, but also minds and souls. Then you have a secret group of people who have seen through the lie of the world and who fight to free humanity from its shackles. Remember the Oracle and her group of talented kids? She was an Acanthus of the Mysterium. The Pentacle are just what would happen if you really delved into the different factions of people who had Awakened from the Matrix, but didn't really have a Zion to go to.<br /> <br /> Cypher was a Seer sympathizer and recruit.<br /> <br /> Now, you can play Mage while ignoring the Pentacle and the Seers and it's still a great game. You can totally be a mage from a cultural Tradition exploring the Shadow, but you did ask me to sell you on specifically the Pentacle and the Seers.<br /> <br /> And if you want something based on real life people, the Seers are as human as you can get. Look around at society and tell me that most people wouldn't support a theoretically corrupt government as long as it kept them fed, housed, and entertained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:30:46-07:00","id":609786,"title":"","content":"I was always a fan of Mage: The Ascencion. Well, certainly I don't expect the same game. But Requiem and Forsaken didn't disapointed me.<br /> <br /> Mage came with some really neat stuff. I had some minor issues with the magic system, but I really liked it overall. I like the idea of True Magic and of a splat with Dynamic power.<br /> <br /> The take on the origin of True Magic being Plato-inspired was an interesting twist, if not all that unexpected. Again, I liked it.<br /> <br /> So you can see that I do like a lot of things in Mage.<br /> <br /> But them things start to go sour. The Watchtowers aren't all that bad. I think they could be a bit more freeform, with the five presented being common, but more open to possibilities. But i can live with that.<br /> <br /> Atlantis went too far, though. Nothing against this kind of legend by itself. The problem was how pervasive it was on the setting.<br /> <br /> When I see a line for WoD, one of the things I like is to imagine all kind of people turning into this splat and figuring out things by themselfs. Mage society isn't comprised by Mages from eons ago, but by people Awakening today. So... why should anyone follow those stories and those orders? Why this society works that way? And all I saw in the core book of 1st ed was a bunch of orders strongly based on a mythic society no one remembers, that only make sense in the context they create to themselfs. And it failed to convince me that a recently Awakened would join most of them, even less believe in all its ideas. It failed to convince me that someone who Awakened to true power would even care about them or pay any attention. The Seers should be the major order, but they seem even worse.<br /> <br /> For me, it killed the setting. And that's a shame. It seemed all the potential for the line just falled. It could be so much more. In some respects, Ascension seems to me much more nWoD-like than Awakening. Awakening seems more like D&amp;D with bad combat rules.<br /> <br /> Yet, there are a lot of fans for this game. So I saw evidence that maybe I just misinterpreted the game, or it changed for the better with time. But I don't have much time and when I remember the 1st core the will to read more books vanishes. I started to read the blogs about the Orders, and a do liked most of the content, tough not everything, but that's ok. Just not enough yet to get rid of my Atlantis problem. And the Seers seem as silly to me now as they seemed back them. The new take on the Orders seem good, but the core principle of the pentacle is still devoid of appeal or sense to me.<br /> <br /> Now I'm here. In another thread the OP asked for reasons to play Changeling: The Dreaming. It is an interesting thread and gave me the idea. I just wanted to see what the fans had to say about the game. Sorry if this was so annoying.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hadn't saw Ophidimancer's post before mine. It started to help, actualy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 07-31-2015, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:36:48-07:00","id":609789,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the Free Council is the place for you, then. Fuck the Diamond and their Atlantean bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:52:45-07:00","id":609800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... why should anyone follow those stories and those orders?</div> </div> </div> </div> Most people who Awaken had no inkling of magic before and no sense or certainty about what has happened to them or what can be done with it. The Orders are a system of education and context and an established set of beliefs of cosmology and purpose. People can join Orders because they come forward to explain and assist in this uncanny and terrifying time in your life. People can believe in the Order philosophies because it makes sense with what they've experienced and resonates with what they might have done before, or what their Obsessions may turn out to be. Look at what the Second Edition previews say about what kind of person joins the Orders. You're hardly ever going to Awaken and think that there's nothing else you might have to figure out about the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:58:42-07:00","id":609805,"title":"","content":"@Monteparnas: Do you realize that Atlantis is just a convenient myth that is used as a metaphor of The Time Before? No one takes it as gospel truth, not even the Silver Ladder and they're the ones who started that trend.<br /> <br /> Are you aware that it's perfectly alright to not join an Order if you're okay with being severely disadvantaged by your lack of resources, contacts and lore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:06:40-07:00","id":609810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609786#post609786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atlantis went too far, though. Nothing against this kind of legend by itself. The problem was how pervasive it was on the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it help at all that Atlantis is going to be de-emphasized in 2ed? Also that Atlantis was never supposed to be a real objective fact of the setting, but rather a mythic ideal that the Orders use as a praxis to structure their ideals and magic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609786#post609786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I see a line for WoD, one of the things I like is to imagine all kind of people turning into this splat and figuring out things by themselfs. Mage society isn't comprised by Mages from eons ago, but by people Awakening today. So... why should anyone follow those stories and those orders?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orders don't generally behave like they live in a Rennaissance Faire all the time. They're perfectly modern, they just think they have ancient roots. It's more about the ethos in the modern day that convince people to join. People don't join the Adamantine Arrow because they believe they are ancient warriors, they join because they want to improve themselves by sparring with the universe and think that people need protecting. People join the Silver Ladder because they see how weird and disorganized people get when they realize they can use magic to get whatever they want and think the people could accomplish so much more if they worked together. Among other reasons, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609786#post609786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why this society works that way? And all I saw in the core book of 1st ed was a bunch of orders strongly based on a mythic society no one remembers, that only make sense in the context they create to themselfs. And it failed to convince me that a recently Awakened would join most of them, even less believe in all its ideas. It failed to convince me that someone who Awakened to true power would even care about them or pay any attention. The Seers should be the major order, but they seem even worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you looked closely at the tenets, the core beliefs, of each of the Orders? None of them necessitate that you believe in Atlantis. I see people joining them on the strengths of their ethical beliefs, Atlantis aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:16:52-07:00","id":609820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609667#post609667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's not for you. I don't really care for Werewolf the Apocalypse personally though I can definitely see there's lots of well written stuff in it. If you've read the core book and you just don't like it, I'm not seeing what help you're expecting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say though that the core book of mage is not very good. I needed to read Tome of Mysteries to really get mage in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609786#post609786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was always a fan of Mage: The Ascencion. Well, certainly I don't expect the same game. But Requiem and Forsaken didn't disapointed me.<br /> <br /> Mage came with some really neat stuff. I had some minor issues with the magic system, but I really liked it overall. I like the idea of True Magic and of a splat with Dynamic power.<br /> <br /> The take on the origin of True Magic being Plato-inspired was an interesting twist, if not all that unexpected. Again, I liked it.<br /> <br /> So you can see that I do like a lot of things in Mage.<br /> <br /> But them things start to go sour. The Watchtowers aren't all that bad. I think they could be a bit more freeform, with the five presented being common, but more open to possibilities. But i can live with that.<br /> <br /> Atlantis went too far, though. Nothing against this kind of legend by itself. The problem was how pervasive it was on the setting.<br /> <br /> When I see a line for WoD, one of the things I like is to imagine all kind of people turning into this splat and figuring out things by themselfs. Mage society isn't comprised by Mages from eons ago, but by people Awakening today. So... why should anyone follow those stories and those orders? Why this society works that way? And all I saw in the core book of 1st ed was a bunch of orders strongly based on a mythic society no one remembers, that only make sense in the context they create to themselfs. And it failed to convince me that a recently Awakened would join most of them, even less believe in all its ideas. It failed to convince me that someone who Awakened to true power would even care about them or pay any attention. The Seers should be the major order, but they seem even worse.<br /> <br /> For me, it killed the setting. And that's a shame. It seemed all the potential for the line just falled. It could be so much more. In some respects, Ascension seems to me much more nWoD-like than Awakening. Awakening seems more like D&amp;D with bad combat rules.<br /> <br /> Yet, there are a lot of fans for this game. So I saw evidence that maybe I just misinterpreted the game, or it changed for the better with time. But I don't have much time and when I remember the 1st core the will to read more books vanishes. I started to read the blogs about the Orders, and a do liked most of the content, tough not everything, but that's ok. Just not enough yet to get rid of my Atlantis problem. And the Seers seem as silly to me now as they seemed back them. The new take on the Orders seem good, but the core principle of the pentacle is still devoid of appeal or sense to me.<br /> <br /> Now I'm here. In another thread the OP asked for reasons to play Changeling: The Dreaming. It is an interesting thread and gave me the idea. I just wanted to see what the fans had to say about the game. Sorry if this was so annoying.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hadn't saw Ophidimancer's post before mine. It started to help, actualy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Atlantis is the bigger flaw of Awakening. The creator said he wanted a name that didnt inspired an specific time or place which failed to take into account things from the Movie Atlantis to Aquaman/namor and assume that people were really into the atlantean mythos prominent in the 70s.......i dont get it either. Lemuria or the &quot;awakened city&quot; or even Babel would have being better <br /> <br /> So your problem with mage is why would someone believe in Atlantis when i sound so remove from anything else? They dont.<br /> <br /> The silver ladder who are the most &quot;pro atlantis&quot; recognize that Atlantis is just a social construct to band mages together. I would recommend the reading &quot;tome of mysteries&quot; if that is the best book of mage which is a ST companion kinda book.<br /> <br /> So you say why someone who just awaken would follow the legends? If they had 2 funtional brain cells they wont believe the whole Atlantis, it sound silly as hell like the noddist in masquerade (both are right OOC but still they sound like conspiracy theorist. Your mage would probably not believe Atlantis but he could get behind one of the orders aims. They got beyond Atlantis.<br /> <br /> The order offers you help and training and goal that some people might follow. And the order books give you idea for cultural color the orders to distance from Atlantis. The mysterium for example is an indu-greek tradition in their corebook.<br /> <br /> The silver ladder philosophy run counter to tropes in tales which in itself is interesting. My advice is read the read Tome of Mysteries and tune out the word Atlantis from everybook and its a nice game. Tome of mysteries for example says that instead of chanting in atlantean the high speech can be in normal languages so you can have thing like a mage enchanting in enochian.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beside in thread in another forum, the creator of 2e say there is only 29 mentions of atlantis in the new book and they keep getting less and less with each review. Just 29 more to go!!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:21:14-07:00","id":609865,"title":"","content":"I see how strange can seem an organization built around a mythical concept of a &quot;long lost / has to come&quot; civilization and with the goal (among others) to live even today by its mythical tenets... Who would join such groups?<br /> Then i look around and see a lot of priests, noons and religious people doing exacly that thing... And i doubt someone has first hand experience or even second hand knowladge of what happened 2000 years ago (for christians) or even earlier (for Jews).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","name":"Nirgal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:26:43-07:00","id":609869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, a comment from the developer about Atlantis:</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, indeed. Tough it did worked by removing Atlantis from the place it was put in 1st core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like the Free Council is the place for you, then. Fuck the Diamond and their Atlantean bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, turns out when you only see one Order as making sense, and this very Order is dedicated to prove the others don't, it seems still very poor for a setting. But at least it is a beginning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people who Awaken had no inkling of magic before and no sense or certainty about what has happened to them or what can be done with it. The Orders are a system of education and context and an established set of beliefs of cosmology and purpose. People can join Orders because they come forward to explain and assist in this uncanny and terrifying time in your life. People can believe in the Order philosophies because it makes sense with what they've experienced and resonates with what they might have done before, or what their Obsessions may turn out to be. Look at what the Second Edition previews say about what kind of person joins the Orders. You're hardly ever going to Awaken and think that there's nothing else you might have to figure out about the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are quite right, but it can only go so far. In 1st core I could see no other reason to join the Orders. One implication of this was that only the Mysterium and the Free Council seemed like reasonable choices for anyone given a choice indeed. The Adamantine Arrow, as an example, was just the &quot;Atlantean Army&quot;. Why the f* would I join an army after Awakening!? And one dedicated to a war that didn't even made sense, let alone be one I would want to get involved.<br /> <br /> And after some time, you aren't a newbie anymore. Them you CAN look for like-minded people and get out of your previous allegiance to build up one that does make some sense. With all human history behind, there was plenty of time for Awakened society to figure out something better.<br /> <br /> But that was 1st core. 2nd core seems to be best by far in that regard. Now I can see someone choosing wholeheartedly to join the Orders as they are, tough I'm not sure to what degree. I expect the part about fringe orders to be really good. More than any other splat, Mage needs space for regional culture to flourish over the fictional one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Monteparnas: Do you realize that Atlantis is just a convenient myth that is used as a metaphor of The Time Before? No one takes it as gospel truth, not even the Silver Ladder and they're the ones who started that trend.<br /> <br /> Are you aware that it's perfectly alright to not join an Order if you're okay with being severely disadvantaged by your lack of resources, contacts and lore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you ever read 1st ed core? As I said, 2nd ed development are going the right way, I mainly wanted to see what the fans like in the game. And maybe some tidbits from sources outside the core, because it was the core that make me avoid Mage.<br /> <br /> In 1st ed core too much things are linked to Atlantis. It is just a convenient myth? Probably, but the Orders didn't thought so. The actual myth took a good part of the book, and everything in the Orders related directly to it. That was the part that made no sense back them. They DO took it as gospel truth, EVEN the Free Council, they just thought the past could be left alone in the past. Ok, that isn't entirely true for the F-C, but too near from truth.<br /> <br /> Just think now that minor Orders should't be so disadvanteged as they say, or not at all. I can hardly see the need for the main Orders to be the only good choices by canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I get to your problems I'll go with the sell. You specifically asked how the Pentacle and the Seers can work together to make a modern drama/horror game? Well, did you like the Matrix and the world it posited? Because you have all those elements: A secret, world spanning, conspiracy that controls not just the government, but everyone's fundamental understanding of reality as it is. A conspiracy that is not content to rule people's wallets and homes, but also minds and souls. Then you have a secret group of people who have seen through the lie of the world and who fight to free humanity from its shackles. Remember the Oracle and her group of talented kids? She was an Acanthus of the Mysterium. The Pentacle are just what would happen if you really delved into the different factions of people who had Awakened from the Matrix, but didn't really have a Zion to go to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could work, tough I can't say it appeals to me as the main conflict of the setting, but that I can live with. But the Seers as conspirators... I think I'm really missing something here, because they still look rather foolish and silly to be effective conspirators. They're too... stupid, really. And also too numerous for their supposed beliefs and role. A conspiracy with just a Inner Circle of true conspirators and ignorant servitors works well, but a huge onion of mad cultists backstabbers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, you can play Mage while ignoring the Pentacle and the Seers and it's still a great game. You can totally be a mage from a cultural Tradition exploring the Shadow, but you did ask me to sell you on specifically the Pentacle and the Seers.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. To be precise, I want to sell me Mage-as-Setting (Mage-as-Rule I already bought), but those are focus on the setting, either way. But indeed, now that you touch the subject, I thought since the beginning that Mage should focus more on cultural Tradition. Not in the sense of trying to make a lot of traditions based on specific cultures, I can see from far away such an idea resulting in cathastrophic approaches. But exploring more how Awakenings relate to regional culture and it shapes Awakened societies. A bit more of anthropology would be great in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah Atlantis is the bigger flaw of Awakening. The creator said he wanted a name that didnt inspired an specific time or place which failed to take into account things from the Movie Atlantis to Aquaman/namor and assume that people were really into the atlantean mythos prominent in the 70s.......i dont get it either. Lemuria or the &quot;awakened city&quot; or even Babel would have being better</div> </div> </div> </div>How can I put this? I DID were in the right mythos. Changing to Lemuria, Hi-Brazil, Hyperborea, or whatever wouldn't help. My problem wasn't with the link with the sunken city of comics or the Disney movie. My problem was with the pervasiveness of the myth in 1st core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say though that the core book of mage is not very good. I needed to read Tome of Mysteries to really get mage in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Locating it, that's the problem, and its a huge one. And my other reason to make this thread, since I know a lot of other people who didn't liked the Atlantis thing and can see he issue being answered here. But truth is, the core book HAVE to sell the game. And have to do this well, for two reasons. First because it is the main door to the line. People will make contact with the game through it. They will decide on looking for other sources or not based upon it. Second because sometimes other sourcebooks will never make it to their stores. It is easy to american readers to think all sourcebooks are available. I'm not from an english speaker country, and a lot of Onyx Path's customers nowadays aren't, either. And them a good core book becomes something even more important. It will be the only book for some of us, and for others to put our hands on sourcebooks is so hard that the core have to sell the game very, very well. And 1st ed core Mage was, setting-wise... crappy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:49:08-07:00","id":609899,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I think you're placing more importance on Atlantis than was actually there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:03:14-07:00","id":609919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now I'm here. In another thread the OP asked for reasons to play Changeling: The Dreaming. It is an interesting thread and gave me the idea. I just wanted to see what the fans had to say about the game. Sorry if this was so annoying. </div> </div> </div>I haven't read that particular thread, but even on a good day these usually degenerate into bitter arguments really quickly. That is, when the thread creator isn't just actively trying to persuade people that the game they like is actually terrible. Like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And 1st ed core Mage was, setting-wise... crappy. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:08:45-07:00","id":609923,"title":"","content":"My bad, but I said because I know most people started to really enjoy Mage with sourcebooks. I want to know about the setting as it is now (before 2nd is released).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:10:40-07:00","id":609924,"title":"","content":"As someone who started out with the same idea as the OP (Why the F would I join any of these?) let me try and help you:<br /> <br /> Why would you join?<br /> Because you don't know better.<br /> <br /> You Awaken, you finally understand how the world truly works, you have cosmic powers able to bend space and time....and then it hits you like a truck - am I alone? Am I mad? What should I do with this power?<br /> <br /> And then someone finds you. She's kind, warm-hearted, friendly. She teaches you the basics of what's going on, tells you you ain't alone, presents you to other Mages. She invites you to party, she tells you how great it is that she was the first to find you, because the others wouldn't have been so kind.<br /> You see, the Adamantine Arrow are murderous warriors thinking of Magic only as a weapon.<br /> Then there's the Mysterium, thinking of others as tools in their researches.<br /> The Free Council, anarchists and rebels.<br /> The Silver Ladder, devoted to open this power to everyone on earth, rather than making sure that only wise people get this gift.<br /> The Seers of the Throne, those who conspire behind layers and layers of lies and trickeries, those who want to keep the Magic to themselves beyond everything. Fear them the most.<br /> <br /> And then there's us - The Guardians of the Veil. We, your friends. Come, we have so much to teach you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now take this story and bend it towards every order, including the Seers, and you'll see how easy it is to gather mages in your order. You don't explain the fundaments behind every other order - you make the new guy fear the others and teach him why they should like <i>you.</i> What's <i>your </i>goal - not theirs, you couldn't care less about what the Mysterium does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:14:31-07:00","id":610019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609869#post609869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are quite right, but it can only go so far. In 1st core I could see no other reason to join the Orders. One implication of this was that only the Mysterium and the Free Council seemed like reasonable choices for anyone given a choice indeed. The Adamantine Arrow, as an example, was just the &quot;Atlantean Army&quot;. Why the f* would I join an army after Awakening!? And one dedicated to a war that didn't even made sense, let alone be one I would want to get involved.<br /> <br /> And after some time, you aren't a newbie anymore. Them you CAN look for like-minded people and get out of your previous allegiance to build up one that does make some sense. With all human history behind, there was plenty of time for Awakened society to figure out something better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is not the &quot;Atlantean army&quot; is the &quot;guys who used magic to fight. You can awaken and this guys help you and train you to purge your neighberhood from drug dealers or whatnot. They dont reclute people to fight the seers from the get go mostly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609869#post609869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could work, tough I can't say it appeals to me as the main conflict of the setting, but that I can live with. But the Seers as conspirators... I think I'm really missing something here, because they still look rather foolish and silly to be effective conspirators. They're too... stupid, really. And also too numerous for their supposed beliefs and role. A conspiracy with just a Inner Circle of true conspirators and ignorant servitors works well, but a huge onion of mad cultists backstabbers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think they are stupid?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609869#post609869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Locating it, that's the problem, and its a huge one. And my other reason to make this thread, since I know a lot of other people who didn't liked the Atlantis thing and can see he issue being answered here. But truth is, the core book HAVE to sell the game. And have to do this well, for two reasons. First because it is the main door to the line. People will make contact with the game through it. They will decide on looking for other sources or not based upon it. Second because sometimes other sourcebooks will never make it to their stores. It is easy to american readers to think all sourcebooks are available. I'm not from an english speaker country, and a lot of Onyx Path's customers nowadays aren't, either. And them a good core book becomes something even more important. It will be the only book for some of us, and for others to put our hands on sourcebooks is so hard that the core have to sell the game very, very well. And 1st ed core Mage was, setting-wise... crappy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont get this, you ask us to sell you Mage awakening 1ed or Mage awakening\u00b4s core rulebook? Because the corebook as you said, setting wise was lacking. Bear in mind that they try to fit in one rulebook, magic system, setting, a city example, antagonist and Spirit rules, its more than most cores had to fit in their limited word count and something suffered. The core rulebook was betting that people will buy the atlantis myth from the get go so they didnt though much about putting alternatives for the people who didnt.<br /> <br /> As a whole gameline, the orders are as removed from atlantis as you want them to be, they have points of origin and cultural trappings that you can make them and not even once have the use the &quot;awakened city&quot; as a concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:15:42-07:00","id":610020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Adamantine Arrow, as an example, was just the &quot;Atlantean Army&quot;. Why the f* would I join an army after Awakening!?</div> </div> </div> </div> Existence is War. Enlightenment is Honour. Adaptability is Strength. The Supernal is the Self. Service is Mastery. These are the truths of this world, and you will bow before them, you pigs in human clothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:23:49-07:00","id":610026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609869#post609869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Locating it, that's the problem, and its a huge one. And my other reason to make this thread, since I know a lot of other people who didn't liked the Atlantis thing and can see he issue being answered here. But truth is, the core book HAVE to sell the game. And have to do this well, for two reasons. First because it is the main door to the line. People will make contact with the game through it. They will decide on looking for other sources or not based upon it. Second because sometimes other sourcebooks will never make it to their stores. It is easy to american readers to think all sourcebooks are available. I'm not from an english speaker country, and a lot of Onyx Path's customers nowadays aren't, either. And them a good core book becomes something even more important. It will be the only book for some of us, and for others to put our hands on sourcebooks is so hard that the core have to sell the game very, very well. And 1st ed core Mage was, setting-wise... crappy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry you feel that way, your issues with the corebook were addressed in other books. I'm sorry you have trouble getting your hands on other books, but you probably shouldn't let your view of the 1e corebook continue to embitter you when we try to help you out and explain how things are not actually as bad as you perceived them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:27:00-07:00","id":610031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now take this story and bend it towards every order, including the Seers, and you'll see how easy it is to gather mages in your order. You don't explain the fundaments behind every other order - you make the new guy fear the others and teach him why they should like you. What's your goal - not theirs, you couldn't care less about what the Mysterium does.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's kind of weird that you use the Guardians as the example for this, because they're the ones who make a huge thing out of finding recruits for the other Orders. It's part of their role in the Diamond, part of a juxtaposition between their need to draw people into the Labyrinth and be extremely discerning about who they take on, and part of their self-effacing. It's quite possible that many Guardians will have reservations against trying to bias people against other Orders <i>even for ideal recruits</i>, if only because there can be a tendency to think it's nicer to not try and bring people in; Guardians don't think it's a happy thing to be one of them. Hell, if the only way you could get somebody in is to create a biased image of the other Orders to turn people against them... do you even <i>want</i> a person like that? Guardians need commitment; you don't get commitment from somebody who is only with you because you misrepresented the alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:29:38-07:00","id":610033,"title":"","content":"Well, it might not be perfect for the Guardians, I admit. The idea stays, though? You join the orders not because you have to pick, but because you're osrt-of lost into all this, and dangers are around you, and you're looking for people to share that newfound knowledge","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:07:55-07:00","id":610063,"title":"","content":"I think there's a difference between &quot;in an unfamiliar situation that you can't really relate to regular people, there can be something compelling and genuinely convincing in a set of developed, sophisticated philosophies that provide answers and purpose&quot; and &quot;Orders basically trick you into joining them&quot;. More Buddhism than Scientology, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:30:36-07:00","id":610183,"title":"","content":"Looking back, there's a lot of begging the question at work in several replies; the question &quot;why doesn't anybody in the Diamond get together and come up with something better than the Diamond&quot; has not established its premise of what exactly is wrong with the Diamond, beyond a vague assertion that nobody would want to do any of their things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:25:52-07:00","id":610229,"title":"","content":"I started this game late when a new person joined my gaming group and brought the blue book and requiem with a request that we try it. I said I was game, so they handed me the books and asked if I could have a game ready the next week. Thus was born the vampire Nazi hunters, yea I made a lot of mistakes. I stumbled across mage while searching the net for ideas on opponents and was taken in by the first magic system that actually felt like you were playing a wizards instead of somebody with a bunch of neat, static tricks. I started with only the core, bought online, and like you found the brief descriptions of the setting somewhat lacking.<br /> The history of Atlantis I decided was shaped more by the new age myth than the other way around, instead the real Atlantis was made up of only two truths:<br /> 1-There is a common written language that is found hidden in relics of the ancient world on every continent and in every known culture.<br /> 2-There are supernal relics of the ancient world that modern mages cannot recreate.<br /> That's it, two facts that became embedded in the sleeper mysticism the newly awakened were already familiar with. I figure the awakened version of Atlantis started like this:<br /> Hoary old master to new apprentice: I will teach you about the first city, now lost with only fragments to prove its existence.<br /> Apprentice: Hey, I've heard of that. You're talking about Atlantis right?<br /> Sound of a hard slap to the head.<br /> Master: No! I'm not talking about some Sleeper bull designed to sell the gullible books! I'm talking about the first civilization founded on knowledge of the supernal.<br /> Year later the now former apprentice meets another mage of his generation and talk turns to their experience with their teachers, to which one of them says : I always thought it sounded like the story of Atlantis.<br /> That's it, familiar sleeper mysticism meets awakened archaeology and Atlantis is born. That's only in the European west, in Asia they argue about an entirely different mythology and so do the native Americans. Who knows what the original cultures of Africa and Australia believe, they didn't have much in the way of written records beyond the symbols of the common language hidden among their art.<br /> As for the orders, you awaken to magic and a whole new social circle.<br /> You discover that dark horrors exist in the world and so like the thousands who join police forces and sleeper armies every day you join the Arrows to protect those you care about. In time you internalize this new sub culture, just like those police officers and soldiers.<br /> You were always fascinated by history and exotic cultures and now you learn there are secrets hidden in human history, so with visions of Indiana Jones dancing through your head you join the Mysterium and their sub culture.<br /> You were class president, or a cheerleader, or just a bleeding heart activist and now you meet like minded people who actually have the power to make the world a better place, so you join the Ladder.<br /> Let's face it, you were always something of a paranoid nut case and that was before you knew there really were things in the shadows that wanted to suck your brain out through your nose. You join the Guardians and get your decoder ring.<br /> Awakening didn't really change your outlook on life, it just made you one of the smart people. Steve Jobs ain't got nothing on you so you join the Council and become part of the nerd herd.<br /> You are a member of a superior group of people, or maybe you just really want stuff, so you put on your white sheet, snappy uniform, gang colors, what ever replaces your morals and justifies your crimes, you join a Seer group. Belief in the Exarchs was an option I chose to drop.<br /> Normal people join cliques all the time and the awakened are still just people. Even the outsiders who all sit at the same table because they aren't welcome at any of the others.<br /> I've played games long enough that house ruling a system or setting is now reflex and this was my take on the core setting outlined in the first book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:43:25-07:00","id":610241,"title":"","content":"Perhaps listen to or read broken diamond by Mr DaveB Its an incredible actual play. its what convinced me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?279847-Actual-Play-Mage-The-Awakening-The-Broken-Diamond-(contains-Reign-of-the-Exarchs\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...of-the-Exarchs</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/610129-broken-diamond-by-daveb-converted-to-mp3-by-ivona-reader\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...y-ivona-reader</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T00:09:23-07:00","id":610514,"title":"","content":"<b>monteparnas</b>, I will solve your problems with Atlantis in <b>Mage</b> with only one comic book sheet ( well, two, first for a easier reading of whole context ) from official inspiriation of gameline - prequels to <i><b>Books of Magic</b></i>, by Neil Gaiman. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/d6s1VYc.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/zMQ9pDk.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> There you go! Atlantis is <b><i>Symbol of Art</i></b>, common Shadow Name that Diamond Order use in their rhetoric. It's also a First Civilization Awakened build and modern mages uncover. And it's also non-existing now in time line. It's all of this and non of this. It one of most basic Mysteries of the universe, that Awakened want to solve from thousands of years. Hopes it helps! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-12-2016, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T00:31:11-07:00","id":610518,"title":"","content":"pics aren't loading Wyrd <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> which pages from BoM ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T00:34:41-07:00","id":610519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=610518#post610518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">pics aren't loading Wyrd <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> which pages from BoM ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The page that is quoted in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-fate-of-atlantis-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">the blog entry</a>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neil Gaiman, The Books of Magic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where Humanity gets it wrong, by your time, is in imagining Atlantis as having any kind of quantifiable existence. Which of course it hasn\u2019t; not in the way they imagine, anyway. There have been an awful lot of Atlantises, will be quite a few more.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s just a symbol. A symbol of the art.<br /> <br /> The True Atlantis is inside you, just as it\u2019s inside all of us. The sunken land beneath the dark sea, lost beneath the waves of wet, black stories and myths that break upon the shores of our minds. Atlantis is the Shadow-land. The birth-place of civilization. The fair land in the west that is lost to us, but remains forever, true birthplace and true goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:19:12-07:00","id":610623,"title":"","content":"Magnum Opus, I can see the &quot;trick the newbie&quot; thing happening and working, but only so far. As a body of Mages, an institution, can't figure this strategy really holding things.<br /> <br /> LokiRavenSpeak, I think they're stupid because their entire cult seems pointless. The Seers are described as extremely tied to once-mage-now-gods that visit them in dreams, and as pragmatic conspirators that live in luxury, and as backstabbing powermongers who can't help but work against one another all the time. And it all doesn't sums up very well to me. Of course, religions do exist IRL, and some do get new followers with promisses of riches. Secret societies that work for self improvement and have a mystical bent are a trope, for sure. But in the Seers we have one that is described as much more based on wacky dreams than initiation, too fractured to actualy work, and at the same time simply hugely widespread for no seeming reason. They could be smaller (good conspiracies don't need to be so huge), less based on dreams about too-humane gods.<br /> <br /> I have the impression that they tried to build a foe that could be at the same time optional and overwhelming, but to me it failed on both. They are everywhere and are too ineffective to be a threat.<br /> <br /> Well, I kind of missed my own point. I want to try and play Mage, but at the same time the 1st core let a truly bad impression on me. The only sourcebook I really read was the one about the Abyss with several ideas of Abyssal intrusions. I like the Abyss, much more than I ever liked the cWoD Consensus, as the source of Paradox. But I am liking most of the changes I'm seeing they did through time in the line. As an exemple, the Adamantine Arrow as the Atlantean Army from 1st core is lame, but I REALLY like the take on them as people who understand conflict as a source of knowledge over the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry you feel that way, your issues with the corebook were addressed in other books. I'm sorry you have trouble getting your hands on other books, but you probably shouldn't let your view of the 1e corebook continue to embitter you when we try to help you out and explain how things are not actually as bad as you perceived them to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actualy that's precisely why the thread. To move on and see what I'm missing. And I'm liking most of what I'm seeing. But the 1st core still embitter me not just because it took me away from Mage, but because I'm not the only one. Next step is to translate matherial to some friends, and some of them are really hard to change minds when they make theirs.<br /> <br /> The images from the pages of BoM are broken, that's a shame. Neil Gaiman is always good, and I think I didn't read the prequel of BoM yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:36:44-07:00","id":610630,"title":"","content":"If you want a reason for a new mage to join the Adamantine arrow, How about this?<br /> <br /> You are now aware of the true nature of the world. Honestly, it's a bit of a shithole, with monsters crawling everywhere. How would you like to learn how to punch them in the face? And maybe protect people you care about from the things that go bump in the night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T04:29:29-07:00","id":610653,"title":"","content":"The Seers:<br /> <br /> It's very easy to sell out. It's almost impossible not to sell out to survive in some more capitalistic societies. I don't believe in what the last three companies I worked for do. But I tell myself that it's better to have a job and get paid than shake my fist at the skyscrapers these companies are headquartered in from a place living under a bridge somewhere. For-profit whatever is here to stay in America. It's not going anywhere. You compromise, but it takes a piece of you.<br /> <br /> Now imagine that you Awake to this great power. Suddenly there is potential and possibility. You could do anything. Except someone got there first and they don't like sharing. Since Awakening, you can see the signs everywhere: Someone took this power and made themselves a throne. Of course they did. And they don't want to share.<br /> <br /> They're offering you anything you want, you just have to help them try to close the door behind you, to help them horde this wonderful power. If you do, they can give you more tantalizing knowledge than anyone else. They control reality now. You can't fight that. Why would you want to? You compromise, then compromise a little more.<br /> <br /> The Seers are about finding that guy that sold out, or that part of you that thinks it would be easier to sell out, and externalize it as a villain you can punch in the face or fry with a lightning bolt. That's how it feels to me In 2nd edition so far.<br /> <br /> Not sure if that helps you or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2205-abaddon","name":"Abaddon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T04:32:06-07:00","id":610656,"title":"","content":"Really, when looking on the Arrow in terms of the &quot;cultural role&quot; side rather than the &quot;fully cohesive philosophy&quot; one, they kind of encompass a whole range of vocations that incorporate stress and risk and putting the wellbeing of others over yourself. If your mage is the kind of person who actually willingly, voluntarily became something like an actual soldier, or a police officer, or a firefighter, or a paramedic, or a pro bono defence attorney, or a social worker, etc., they might just gravitate towards the Order that not only does similar things as a matter of course, but preaches the ideal of struggle and service and sacrifice as a method of self-perfection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T05:40:00-07:00","id":610703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening#post609622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atlantis and the Pentacle never had any appeal to me. And the Seers seem just like a bunch of lunatics that I can pretty much ignore. Because seriously, they're just nuts. And not even in a dangerous way.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then... don't use them? Despite some people insisting that the Seers and Exarchs are the primary antagonist of Mages, that's simply not true. Left Hand Paths, rogue magicians, Intruders from the Abyss, hunting for rare grimoires, living spells, dealing with one of the five or so spirit types... there's a lot of potential plot hooks out there. Atlantis, despite being called a necessary buy in for the game, really only matters for a tiny portion of the game, and that's easily ignored. <br /> <br /> Look up the Tokyo setting on the blog. Orders are basically in the background. We have a focus on a local powerful archmage instead of Atlantis, and the major factions make up stories of said archmage as their guiding principles. Atlantis is a hard fact of the setting. That doesn't make it an exceptionally relevant part of the setting, however. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How those things really play together and with other elements to make this game interesting as a modern drama/horror game based on real life people? </div> </div> </div> How do the stories in the Bible play into stories of real life people? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=609786#post609786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like the idea of True Magic and of a splat with Dynamic power.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nitpick - Awakened magic isn't &quot;True Magic.&quot; This is its own thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But them things start to go sour. The Watchtowers aren't all that bad. I think they could be a bit more freeform, with the five presented being common, but more open to possibilities. But i can live with that. </div> </div> </div> There are plenty of hacks out there for making any combination of Arcana, and more watchtowers, etc. <br /> <br /> That said, I'm actually a fan of the five Paths, if not the Watchtower imagry. Five elements. Five styles of magic, ala the MtG magic wheel. Five types of spirits. These are classics that you'll find throughout any novel or story that includes wizards, witches, psychics, alchemists, necromancers.. these are all iconic and adaptable across the globe. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Atlantis went too far, though. Nothing against this kind of legend by itself. The problem was how pervasive it was on the setting. </div> </div> </div> You're over estimating its impact. Really, its mostly just an explanation for the current state of things. Temples you explore can be from post-Fall magic civilizations. Artifacts can come from sources other than Atlantis. Who cares how the Exarchs ascended to power when the method of fixing the problem (unwork the oppression in the world, including Seers) has nothing to do with Atlantis? Like I said above, Atlantis is like the equivalent of the Mage Book of Genesis. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I see a line for WoD, one of the things I like is to imagine all kind of people turning into this splat and figuring out things by themselfs. Mage society isn't comprised by Mages from eons ago, but by people Awakening today. So... why should anyone follow those stories and those orders? </div> </div> </div> Position of privilege. Who doesn't want to join someone who's got all the goodies? They're the established and dominant &quot;religions&quot; of mage society. When you Awaken, look for answers, who's there to initiate you into the Way, the Truth, and the Light?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T17:56:50-07:00","id":611507,"title":"","content":"I'm totally willing to agree with you that the core puts way too much emphasis on Atlantis, and describes the Orders in a way that probably over-emphasizes the Atlantean caste they claim to draw from. I've found that the descriptions of what the Orders see magic as are much more interesting hooks to what the faction is about, both for myself and new players- not sure if you've seen the blog post about this already, but they are: (source: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/</a>)<ul><li>Adamantine Arrow: Challenge is Magical</li> <li>Free Council: Humanity is Magical</li> <li>Guardians of the Veil: Magic is Fragile</li> <li>Mysterium: Magic is Alive</li> <li>Sliver Ladder: Magic is Humanity\u2019s Birthright</li> <li>Seers of the Throne: Magic is Payment</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I think they make a lot more sense in terms of understanding how mages get recruited, as well as in basing your understanding of each Order, rather than their Atlantean class correspondence. A new mage chooses amongst/joins Orders based on which one they feel does the best job explaining this new thing in their life, magic, in a way that speaks to them. Mages (usually) don't join the Arrow because they want to be soldiers, they join the Arrow because they are willing to buy into the idea that &quot;challenge is magical&quot;; that by pushing yourself, by dedicating yourself to a difficult cause, you can gain the power to change the world.<br /> <br /> Conceptually, for me at least, the rest of the Order flows from that central idea of what magic is. The Arrow believe &quot;Service is Mastery&quot; because they see devoting oneself to another as more challenging and more meaningful than acting solely for one's own sake-- saving the town is a lot harder than saving your own skin. They swear Oaths as a way of challenging themselves to uphold them, to act instead of just hesitating. They volunteer as the primary fighters of mage society because it means lots of opportunities to face challenges. The Silver Ladder comes along and says &quot;you guys represent our symbolic ideal soldier caste in our theoretical utopia!&quot; and the Arrows look up from lifting weights and treating lepers to stick their chins out in contemplation, nod, and say &quot;yeah, alright.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:40:12-07:00","id":611673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abaddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=610653#post610653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seers:<br /> <br /> It's very easy to sell out. It's almost impossible not to sell out to survive in some more capitalistic societies. I don't believe in what the last three companies I worked for do. But I tell myself that it's better to have a job and get paid than shake my fist at the skyscrapers these companies are headquartered in from a place living under a bridge somewhere. For-profit whatever is here to stay in America. It's not going anywhere. You compromise, but it takes a piece of you.<br /> <br /> Now imagine that you Awake to this great power. Suddenly there is potential and possibility. You could do anything. Except someone got there first and they don't like sharing. Since Awakening, you can see the signs everywhere: Someone took this power and made themselves a throne. Of course they did. And they don't want to share.<br /> <br /> They're offering you anything you want, you just have to help them try to close the door behind you, to help them horde this wonderful power. If you do, they can give you more tantalizing knowledge than anyone else. They control reality now. You can't fight that. Why would you want to? You compromise, then compromise a little more.<br /> <br /> The Seers are about finding that guy that sold out, or that part of you that thinks it would be easier to sell out, and externalize it as a villain you can punch in the face or fry with a lightning bolt. That's how it feels to me In 2nd edition so far.<br /> <br /> Not sure if that helps you or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the idea, but couldn't by its development.<br /> <br /> First, we got the Exharcs. And to be honest, I don't like them that much. Maybe it is just because of the 1st core linking them to Atlantis, so I'm wyling to accept them. It would be a little better if they where unknown entities instead of confirmed once-mages.<br /> <br /> Them you got their main system of recruitment: weird dreams. You could surely make a case for the Seers if the Exharcs contacted them a little more directly. It could even be dreams, if at least a little clearer. But no, it is just weird dreams, that different Seers interpret in different ways, so you can't even be sure you know what you are listenning to. It is like if you contacted people through messages codified on the music playing on radio, but you never gave ANYONE the cryptographic instructions to decode. The message is as good as random.<br /> <br /> You go on to how they actualy work, and there you find a huge mess. They aren't just traitorous backstabbers. They are <b>extremely</b> traitorous backstabbers. Without nothing to hold your co-workers from messing with you, even your superiors. Their working system is flawed, ineffective and without garantees. You know what? No, I WON'T work in a company that can't even guarantee that promised payment if I don't steal it from another guy. Sincerely, it isn't about ideals, but simply that theirs is a crappy job offer.<br /> <br /> And you end with sheer numbers that don't make sense. With only the problems above I still can figure this cult existing and working and being dangerous, even if in a more localized level. I could even conceive a less structured organization, in fact an idea instead of a monolithic conspiracy. The Seers could work like the Belial's Brood, not in the sense of short-lived chapters, but an idea that birth chapters here and there, without real conection with one another. Not ideal, but better. But with all the characteristics it have, I can't see this Order being so numerous and simultaneously monolithic. Its already hard to see it as just one of those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then... don't use them? Despite some people insisting that the Seers and Exarchs are the primary antagonist of Mages, that's simply not true. Left Hand Paths, rogue magicians, Intruders from the Abyss, hunting for rare grimoires, living spells, dealing with one of the five or so spirit types... there's a lot of potential plot hooks out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't have other intention. Just wanted to see if I was still missing something about the Seers. I am being convinced about most of the setting through this thread, and I'm probably going to do precisely that, ignore the Seers except as ocasional mad cultists and focus elsewere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:06:15-07:00","id":611713,"title":"","content":"The Exarchs don't recruit through dreams, although I imagine that some Seers may employ such techniques among others.<br /> <br /> You're confusing Seer mages with Prelates. Only some Seers become Prelates. As Dave described, they are like made men in the mafia. They've climbed the institutional ladder, paid their dues, and were willing to sacrifice autonomy for even greater reward. Prelates are the Seers whose dreams are invaded with orders and mandates from the supernal gods. They are also very powerful, protected and influential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:38:00-07:00","id":611767,"title":"","content":"The Exarchs are not confirmed once-Mages, no one knows where they come from. Seers typically believe that Exarchs were once Mages not because they have any proof, but because they hope to become Exarchs in the future.<br /> <br /> As Branford mentions the Seers who get contacted via dreams are the ones with Prelacies, most are recruited the good old fashioned way with propaganda and resources. The dreams by the way are only unclear in methods. Basically, they get a message, &quot;I don't care how you do it, suborn the President.&quot; The only differences in interpretation is how to make that happen.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah they're extremely traitorous to one another but its not unbelievable that people would join in spite of that. I worked in a company that actually made me think about the Seers frequently. The amount of backbiting and bitching was incredible. If it had been run by Seers then I would have been one of the ones who stayed because there's nowhere else to go and I feared being homeless. Plenty others were in it for the money and the opportunity to be an asshole to their employees without suffering consequences. It was a nightmare, but a very successful company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T22:40:14-07:00","id":611896,"title":"","content":"You do know that the total number number of Seers slightly outnumber The Diamond but the Free Council by itself is much larger than either faction taken individually? Why do you think the decision The Nameless made when they said screw you to the Seers was the game changer?<br /> <br /> Basically there aren't a huge number of Seers but the ugly truth is they're like Batman (they have ALL the best toys magic wise and heavy duty mundane connections via wealth and any other temporal perk you care to name).<br /> <br /> That combination is flat out tempting to succumb to and nothing anyone says would convince me in game or anyone in real life life differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 08-02-2015, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T22:51:31-07:00","id":611909,"title":"","content":"The Seers recruit through rather mundane means, actually. The dreams don't really start until you're higher up. In the other hand, the Exarchs do send ochemata to the Fallen World, so we do have more direct proof of their existence at the very least. Again though, they are not confirmed as anything because you don't ever get solid confirmation about anything on the Ascended level. So most of your impressions are a bit off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T06:41:04-07:00","id":612155,"title":"","content":"Just to sum up my issues with Seers before:<br /> 1- Exarchs, the once-mage gods;<br /> 2- Recruitment through The Dream Quest of Unknown Kadath;<br /> 3- Traitorous backstabbers to the point of inneficience;<br /> 4- Sheer numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=611713#post611713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exarchs don't recruit through dreams, although I imagine that some Seers may employ such techniques among others.<br /> <br /> You're confusing Seer mages with Prelates. Only some Seers become Prelates. As Dave described, they are like made men in the mafia. They've climbed the institutional ladder, paid their dues, and were willing to sacrifice autonomy for even greater reward. Prelates are the Seers whose dreams are invaded with orders and mandates from the supernal gods. They are also very powerful, protected and influential.</div> </div> </div> </div>By what I had saw in the 1st core that was their only recruiting process, and nothing in the dev blogs I read until now seemed to change that. But if you say so, one problem less, three remain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the other hand, the Exarchs do send ochemata to the Fallen World, so we do have more direct proof of their existence at the very least. Again though, they are not confirmed as anything because you don't ever get solid confirmation about anything on the Ascended level. So most of your impressions are a bit off.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does make sense, tough I have no idea what an &quot;ochemata&quot; is. If it was in the core, I don't remember. Just two remain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, yeah they're extremely traitorous to one another but its not unbelievable that people would join in spite of that. I worked in a company that actually made me think about the Seers frequently. The amount of backbiting and bitching was incredible. If it had been run by Seers then I would have been one of the ones who stayed because there's nowhere else to go and I feared being homeless. Plenty others were in it for the money and the opportunity to be an asshole to their employees without suffering consequences. It was a nightmare, but a very successful company.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here I will hold back a little, sorry. I do know there are plenty of hellish places to work where money never stop to come. But there ARE limits for it to be feasible. Your company still offered two protections: for the employees, that the money would actualy come most of the time, instead of taken away by corrupt colleagues or superiors. And to the superiors, that they wouldn't have to fear retaliation. And probably they didn't suffered so much from <u>their</u> superiors, so climbing the corporative ladder probably granted some respite. The Seers doesn't seem to offer any of those, and in fact be fractured enough to not even work like a company, but like a lot of them in open war against one another. That's where it becomes extremely innefective. So this problem remains to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know that the total number number of Seers slightly outnumber The Diamond but the Free Council by itself is much larger than either faction taken individually? Why do you think the decision The Nameless made when they said screw you to the Seers was the game changer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet a huge amount of them. I wouldn't mind so much as I do now if they where only the biggest order. But to say they're bigger than the four most traditional orders united!? Even when those orders seemed a bunch of nutjobs to me, it was still a huge number. And the Free Council being even bigger doesn't help things. To me the major power should be the regional minor orders with roots on local culture. The problem, so, remains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That combination is flat out tempting to succumb to and nothing anyone says would convince me in game or anyone in real life life differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first that there IS a limit on the temptation power of that combination, both in game and IRL. Don't forget that the people they are trying to recruit are overpowered Mages themselves, you all seem to forget that when it comes to the Seers. Those &quot;exploited employees&quot; are powerful and full of potential in their own right, prone to Hubris, and so with no reason to NOT refuse all that out of simple mundane pride. There are people like this IRL, and the game assumes right from the start that Mages are like that, with no reason not to be.<br /> <br /> And second, seriously, for more that combination seems tempting, if they don't seem to have the means to make it workable, either they are very unlikely to actualy have that combination to begin with, or they will simply lose it to a more efficient group. The Guardians of the Veil seems much more competent han the Seers in this regard.<br /> <br /> Out of four, two issues where taken, two remain. That's just me keeping personal tabs, though, I will read further explanations, and I do feel the Seers at least usable now. The backstabbing part needs to be toned down a bit, without loss to the feeling of abuse and claustrophobia from within. That's manageable. The size is still to great, but without the other problems it is less of one. And also one I can correct without so much trouble as the two better addressed would have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T08:04:30-07:00","id":612222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to sum up my issues with Seers before:<br /> 3- Traitorous backstabbers to the point of inneficience;<br /> <br /> By what I had saw in the 1st core that was their only recruiting process, and nothing in the dev blogs I read until now seemed to change that. But if you say so, one problem less, three remain.<br /> <br /> It does make sense, tough I have no idea what an &quot;ochemata&quot; is. If it was in the core, I don't remember. Just two remain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here I will hold back a little, sorry. I do know there are plenty of hellish places to work where money never stop to come. But there ARE limits for it to be feasible. Your company still offered two protections: for the employees, that the money would actualy come most of the time, instead of taken away by corrupt colleagues or superiors. And to the superiors, that they wouldn't have to fear retaliation. And probably they didn't suffered so much from <u>their</u> superiors, so climbing the corporative ladder probably granted some respite. The Seers doesn't seem to offer any of those, and in fact be fractured enough to not even work like a company, but like a lot of them in open war against one another. That's where it becomes extremely innefective. So this problem remains to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is mentioned in the Seers devblog what the dreams are used for, handing out missions, not necessarily recruiting. There may be some special Mages that the Exarchs would recruit via dreams but it's by far a very, very small minority.<br /> <br /> Ochemata came out in Imperial Mysteries a book you probably haven't had a chance to read. They're essentially sub-souls of ascended beings and archmasters capable of carrying out the will of the ones who created them in the Fallen world without relying on the direct intervention of such powerful beings themselves.<br /> <br /> As to the risk/reward thing of the Seers: If you can't deliver on the promises of wealth that your followers expect then you don't deserve the position and you get demoted or worse. That's how the Seers guarantee they receive protection and benefits from their higher-ups. Naturally, the higher-ups don't want to be usurped by competent underlings, so they distract their minions by creating dead-end jobs and pointless &quot;promotions&quot; to distract them from the positions of actual power in the Seers. Also if you as a Seer fuck up then you can expect some harsh punishments which are designed to keep you in line and keep you from nipping at your boss' heels for his job. On the flip side the underlings are always watching their boss for a slip up so they can steal their position, power and resources. Those most expected to rise and the hardest to bump out of their positions are the ones who wholly buy into the Seers philosophy and become Prelates or higher in the Seer organization with that access that the Exarchs have to their soul they have a little more security in their position which allows them to flex power outside the Order and sustain slightly more screw-ups (providing badly needed stability of which there isn't ever really enough) which means they're also the most likely to be able to provide those material rewards that Seers expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T08:32:35-07:00","id":612267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=611673#post611673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't have other intention. Just wanted to see if I was still missing something about the Seers. I am being convinced about most of the setting through this thread, and I'm probably going to do precisely that, ignore the Seers except as ocasional mad cultists and focus elsewere.</div> </div> </div> </div> In a way, you are. One of the plots in Mage involves the development of civilization - that's why we constantly see Law-giver, Scholar, Warrior, and Secret Police repeated in Seer, Diamond, FC, and even cabal roles. There's a specific style of plot that you can really only do with a focus on Orders. And the Seers about Order v. Order types of plots.<br /> <br /> If you're not into that kind of plot, then you're not into that kind of plot. I'm not, so the Orders and Seers become less important to me. As you can see here, there are some who like that kind of story, so the Orders are important to them.<br /> <br /> There's a lot we can go into with them, but its not my thing, so I will leave it up to others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just to sum up my issues with Seers before:<br /> 1- Exarchs, the once-mage gods;<br /> 2- Recruitment through The Dream Quest of Unknown Kadath;<br /> 3- Traitorous backstabbers to the point of inneficience;<br /> 4- Sheer numbers. </div> </div> </div> 1. In Mage, a lot of the gods are once-human mages. For instance, the five Oracles that built the Watchtowers are supposedly the five Archangels of christian lore (Michael, Raphael, Gabriel, Uriel, and Lucifer). Is your problem that they're once people that evolved into something else?<br /> <br /> 2. Seers recruit through cults, just like the Guardians of the Veil and their Labrynths, the SL and their Cryptopoly, the Mysterium and their academic circles, etc. Almost every mage has dreams and uses divination tools after their Awakening, to an extent, so the Seers aren't unique in this method.<br /> <br /> 3. There are plenty of people IRL who are like that. Pretty much any kind of cut-throat corporate atmosphere, competing for advancement, showcases this. I hardly think you can call mega-corporations or national politics ineffective. Plus, its not like mass murder is going on here. Vampires are supposedly backstabbers too, but they function well.<br /> <br /> 4. Sheer numbers? I don't recall hearing that the Seers outnumbered the Diamond. They <i>outgun</i> them, absolutely. They've got the better resources, better connections. Don't know about raw numbers, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-02-2015, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:09:57-07:00","id":612314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612267#post612267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. In Mage, a lot of the gods are once-human mages. For instance, the five Oracles that built the Watchtowers are supposedly the five Archangels of christian lore (Michael, Raphael, Gabriel, Uriel, and Lucifer). Is your problem that they're once people that evolved into something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no proof that the Oracles were once people either. That's Silver Ladder propaganda, and heck there's not even a lot of proof that the Oracles exist at all.<br /> <br /> There's definitely nothing I've seen that says the Oracles are supposedly the five archangels of any kind of lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T11:21:59-07:00","id":612434,"title":"","content":"Ok, I just went back and re-read all the Seer stuff in the core, so maybe I can help you a bit more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Exarchs, the once-mage gods;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not confirmed at all. It's just a theory held by the Atlantean orthodoxy. Same as the theory that the Watchtowers are the work of the Oracles and that the Oracles are Atlantean princes. All unconfirmed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- Recruitment through The Dream Quest of Unknown Kadath;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Seers recruit. It's how they send marching orders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3- Traitorous backstabbers to the point of inneficience;</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, they seem to work together as well as the Orders do, but I guess that's just my interpretation. If anything, they seem like a very good pyramid scheme. Sure, they might interfere with each other in the lofty ideals, stuff like interpreting the grand goals of the Exarchs, but on the ground they do at least agree on opposing the Orders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4- Sheer numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one's easy, they have all the money and the creature comforts. Not hard to see why they'd have an easy time recruiting. From what I've gathered, they are bigger than any individual Order, but not bigger than any two, but that could also be my interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does make sense, tough I have no idea what an &quot;ochemata&quot; is. If it was in the core, I don't remember. Just two remain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ochemata are servants of the Exarchs (or any ascended being, really) sent directly to the Fallen World. They weren't in the core, sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet a huge amount of them. I wouldn't mind so much as I do now if they where only the biggest order. But to say they're bigger than the four most traditional orders united!? Even when those orders seemed a bunch of nutjobs to me, it was still a huge number. And the Free Council being even bigger doesn't help things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not exactly the impression I got. It could just be me, but I thought that the Seers were bigger than any one of the Pentacle, but not bigger than two combined. I did get the impression that they were better than the rest at entrenching themselves in government bodies, so perhaps they have greater reach than any of the Orders.<br /> <br /> All the population talk is kind of moot, though, because every Storyteller controls the exact population of mages as they see fit. No one at White Wolf is making any charts as to the exact population of mages because that's left of to the ST at each individual table. The numbers of mages in your setting should serve YOUR story, not the other way around. There isn't some grand unified canon that you MUST adhere to in your story. If you wanted, you don't have to have a Seer presence at all, or perhaps in your city they might outnumber the Pentacle ridiculously to where it's like Neo and Trinity against a bunch of Agents all the time. It's up to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the major power should be the regional minor orders with roots on local culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by minor orders? Because there are such things as smaller orders that aren't the Pentacle. The Pentacle generally calls them Nameless Orders and they are a thing, but they don't have the same kind of support or magical might that the actual Orders have (rotes, artifacts, Merits like Masques or Adamantine Hand) because well ... that's just a conceit of the setting. Rather than being about local Magical Traditions (which are still a thing) it is about globe spanning conspiracies, a term which applies to the Pentacle and the Throne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T11:53:32-07:00","id":612474,"title":"","content":"Actually, I don't understand how you could have the opinion that major power should be held by regional minor orders. If they're regional and so wrapped up in the local culture that they can't expand beyond their cultural borders and draw in more members then of course they won't be able to achieve the kind of power that any of the other actual Orders have. It's like comparing a local banana stand to Chiquita, or a local Japanese shrine to Buddhism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:03:00-07:00","id":612479,"title":"","content":"Yeah, global conspiracies of mages seem kind of inevitable given two things:<br /> 1) Humans are social creatures and generally accomplish greater things working together.<br /> 2) The Space Arcanum means that distance is effectively meaningless to mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:14:32-07:00","id":612592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the major power should be the regional minor orders with roots on local culture.</div> </div> </div> </div> It may sound a bit tautological to say that's not what the game is about, but... it just isn't. Awakening has well developed and well reasoned purpose behind the Orders. It not being to somebody's taste is one thing, but that's really on them. I find the statement &quot;sell me on this thing&quot; to be in rather bad faith if one is just going to dispute and deride everything people try to sell the game with. &quot;Convince me to like this game despite how terrible it is&quot; is a trap, and it's one I'm growing weary of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:32:41-07:00","id":612606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the major power should be the regional minor orders with roots on local culture.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Awakening</b> is game of nWoD lines and as such is made to be very customizable. You can easily run a game when in local area the Nameless Orders ( minor, local magical societies ) are more prominent and Pentacle and Seers are nowhere near here, even after those two and a half thousand years. Hell, it's even mine idea for newbie game for our RPG club when 2ED <b>Mage</b> comes out - players will be a local cult leading cabal, totally Nameless. And then - bum - this pesky Pentacle comes to their town. And with them Seers. And all handful of trouble. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nameless are described in the <b>Left Hand Path</b> book. Also other &quot;dark mages&quot;, like Scelasti, Tremere and Apostates of Pentacle. In 2ED Nameless, both technological and &quot;minor, local orders&quot; are making core of Free Council also.<br /> <br /> For the historical origins of Global Orders, see <i>To the Strongest</i> Chapter of <b>Dark Eras</b> book where Diamond and Seers rose from the Nameless after the Alexander's the Great death. It would show you more how the local Nameless Orders <b>choose </b>to become Global Orders and that most of the time Nameless just <i>join</i> Pentacle or Seers, sooner or later. But in 2ED core one of example characters is the Nameless Order memeber. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-02-2015, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:47:57-07:00","id":612751,"title":"","content":"Okay, so that question about the Seers and what their attraction is and how they function in an environment of constant low-level internecine scheming: does one know what a &quot;corporate executive&quot; is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T15:09:34-07:00","id":614175,"title":"","content":"On the Seers having more numbers than the four traditional Orders: keep in mind that Seers are divided into Ministries, so &quot;Seers&quot; is more akin to the organizational branch that is the Pentacle or Werewolf's Pure Tribes than a given Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T16:19:00-07:00","id":614261,"title":"","content":"Assuming it didn't change:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage Demographics 101<br /> <br /> The largest single group of Mages in the setting is the Free Council.<br /> The smallest Pentacle order is the Guardians of the Veil.<br /> The Seers, all Ministries combined, are the size of two of the middle-sized Pentacle orders.<br /> <br /> That's it. No more has been stated. Mages don't have a &quot;ratio to Sleepers&quot; number like Vampires do.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default67ee-4.html?g=posts&amp;m=1433785#post1433785\" target=\"_blank\">[SOURCE]</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaveB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the book: &quot;The worldwide population of Nameless is about that of a mid-sized Ministry&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default9969-6.html?g=posts&amp;m=1563297#post1563297\" target=\"_blank\">[SOURCE]</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T16:34:08-07:00","id":614277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=614261#post614261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming it didn't change:<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default67ee-4.html?g=posts&amp;m=1433785#post1433785\" target=\"_blank\">[SOURCE]</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default9969-6.html?g=posts&amp;m=1563297#post1563297\" target=\"_blank\">[SOURCE]</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So all we know is:<br /> <br /> FC &gt; Seers = (SL + AA || SL + Mysterium || AA + Mysterium) &gt; SL || Mysterium || AA &gt; GotV<br /> <br /> With all the Nameless combined being either slightly larger than, equal to, or smaller than the GotV, but definitely smaller than the Mysterium, SL, or AA. The exact numbers between the SL, Mysterium, and AA are unknown, and the number of Free Council could be significantly greater than the total Diamond mages (unlikely), equal to, to probably no lower than 2/3 the numbers of the complete Diamond.<br /> <br /> That's <i>very</i> open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T17:29:51-07:00","id":614318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">keep in mind that Seers are divided into Ministries, so &quot;Seers&quot; is more akin to the organizational branch that is the Pentacle or Werewolf's Pure Tribes than a given Order.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's more that there are Ministries within the Seers, while there are still plenty of Seers who belong to no Ministry, their basic geographic establishment tends to be pan-Ministry, and part of the nature of their hierarchy ultimately ties them all together in a convoluted but ultimately comprehensive network. The central commandments of the Seers are not necessarily tied to any given Exarch, so you can have multiple Seers of different creeds all working together on any given one of them, similar with their reward system and perspectives on those rewards. I'd also say that the Ministries are insufficiently different from one another to really be considered as distinct as Diamond Orders or Pure Tribes; on that note alone, I would view the collective as being a form of Order. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all the Nameless combined being either slightly larger than, equal to, or smaller than the GotV</div> </div> </div> </div> I would assume a mid-sized Ministry to be larger than the Guardians myself; I see them as being very exclusive. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the number of Free Council could be significantly greater than the total Diamond mages (unlikely)</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, it's definitely been stated that the Free Council does not outnumber the entire Diamond <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's very open.</div> </div> </div> </div> My take on the significance of those ratios is that it's more to give a sense of how much of a draw any given group is first, an indication of what their internal culture can be like second, and all other concerns are minor enough to be lumped together as a fairly distant third. I feel as though the actual numbers of mages can be adjusted fairly easily, because I tend to assume that a large proportion of mages (which expands or contracts depending on what one views their overall numbers as) tend to fall into a comfortable personal niche at about a mid-level form of power (I'd say the disciple Practices and Supernal summoning are about enough to bend the Arcana towards purposes guaranteeing a life of relative ease), engaging with the Orders and pursuing Mysteries in the manner of membership in a particular subculture, and kind of forming a social and support network to mages of greater activity and ambition. If the Awakened stand as the powerful and priviliged amongst the various subcultures of Sleepwalkers that make up their corner of the World of Darkness, these would be the kinds of people who live off of trust funds or retire early after some major success or windfall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T19:47:57-07:00","id":614434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=614318#post614318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's definitely been stated that the Free Council does not outnumber the entire Diamond</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put it at the entire FC is around 2/3 the size of the entire Diamond in actual Awakened Mages.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T21:57:06-07:00","id":614568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=614434#post614434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd put it at the entire FC is around 2/3 the size of the entire Diamond in actual Awakened Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, FC is the largest but slightly smaller than the Diamond with the Seers likely being smaller than the Diamond and clearly smaller than the FC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 08-04-2015, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T22:19:19-07:00","id":614589,"title":"","content":"Considering that, if it weren't for all the Diamond Orders ganging up, the Free Council could easily shout each of them down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T22:37:43-07:00","id":614594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=614568#post614568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, FC is the largest but slightly smaller than the Diamond with the Seers likely being smaller than the Diamond and clearly smaller than the FC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked 2/3 was less than 1. But I don't know, maybe an archmage changed math or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T22:32:36-07:00","id":617155,"title":"","content":"It is at least possible to have a happy ending in a life without fear, with only the excess baggage you chose to bringbring into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6516-mefathiel8","name":"mefathiel8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T13:48:09-07:00","id":618038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. In Mage, a lot of the gods are once-human mages. For instance, the five Oracles that built the Watchtowers are supposedly the five Archangels of christian lore (Michael, Raphael, Gabriel, Uriel, and Lucifer). Is your problem that they're once people that evolved into something else?<br /> <br /> 2. Seers recruit through cults, just like the Guardians of the Veil and their Labrynths, the SL and their Cryptopoly, the Mysterium and their academic circles, etc. Almost every mage has dreams and uses divination tools after their Awakening, to an extent, so the Seers aren't unique in this method.<br /> <br /> 3. There are plenty of people IRL who are like that. Pretty much any kind of cut-throat corporate atmosphere, competing for advancement, showcases this. I hardly think you can call mega-corporations or national politics ineffective. Plus, its not like mass murder is going on here. Vampires are supposedly backstabbers too, but they function well.<br /> <br /> 4. Sheer numbers? I don't recall hearing that the Seers outnumbered the Diamond. They <i>outgun</i> them, absolutely. They've got the better resources, better connections. Don't know about raw numbers, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- I have a problem with things that don't need canon explanation having canon explanation. That said, knowing that the Exarchs aren't really explained already helped.<br /> <br /> 2- Quite understood that, thank you.<br /> <br /> 3- As I tried to say, it is about balance with enough guarantees for you to make this work worth your effort. By what Mrmdubois said, I think it isn't as stupidly cutthroat as I thought. If it is confirmed, I won't have problems with an unhealthy work environment.<br /> <br /> 4- Well, that's what I consistently heard, though. And even outgunning them so much seems a little too much for me. But as I said, it is more of a problem if the other ones where real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no proof that the Oracles were once people either. That's Silver Ladder propaganda, and heck there's not even a lot of proof that the Oracles exist at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good on my book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by minor orders? Because there are such things as smaller orders that aren't the Pentacle. The Pentacle generally calls them Nameless Orders and they are a thing, but they don't have the same kind of support or magical might that the actual Orders have (rotes, artifacts, Merits like Masques or Adamantine Hand) because well ... that's just a conceit of the setting. Rather than being about local Magical Traditions (which are still a thing) it is about globe spanning conspiracies, a term which applies to the Pentacle and the Throne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad concept by itself. But given the nWoD tone, I think &quot;Global Conspiracy&quot; shouldn't be a core concept. Period. The nWoD was from he beginning about local mystery. In Mage, focus on local orders based on local culture would be much more interesting, the Global Conspiracy being an optional side approach (as it is everywhere else).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I don't understand how you could have the opinion that major power should be held by regional minor orders. If they're regional and so wrapped up in the local culture that they can't expand beyond their cultural borders and draw in more members then of course they won't be able to achieve the kind of power that any of the other actual Orders have. It's like comparing a local banana stand to Chiquita, or a local Japanese shrine to Buddhism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because far from the seats of power of any company, the most powerful locally are usually local businesses. I never heard of Chiquita, don't even know what are you talking about. In my country Giraffas', Habibi's and Truck's are some of the biggest fast food companies, and in no few neighborhoods and small cities the biggest presences are completely local companies you won't hear about four cities away. And both in Buddhism and Catholicism, and actually in any religion, the local priest is by far more influential than any centralized power, when it does exist to begin with. By the way, talking about religion, in a lot of places the bigger and most influential isn't the biggest in a global sense. Or you think the Roman Catholic Church is so more powerful than everyone else in a given city? Because I can guarantee you, they are still the biggest organized religion in the world.<br /> <br /> You should also remember that they being present the world around doesn't mean they are able to pool all resources that way. If they are so spread, that also means a lot of things will never get out of a given Concilium, and that resources have to be split between Concilia. It is made even harder once they don't have centralized all-powerful administration. So even spanning the world around, they ARE local powers. Just local powers with a lot of nominal allies (with their own problems). Even government and centralized companies have a lot of problems with internal organization for you to say they are able to pool all their resources at anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, global conspiracies of mages seem kind of inevitable given two things:<br /> 1) Humans are social creatures and generally accomplish greater things working together.<br /> 2) The Space Arcanum means that distance is effectively meaningless to mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Humans are also insular creatures and rarely care so much for people they don't have any proximal contact. Most people barely cooperate with coworkers in such level.<br /> 2) Continual growth in transport and communication systems also improved our ability to do so without magic, and tough there are considerable advances in our ability to coordinate work, and a lot of people do this with friends far away, it came at the cost of our ability to cooperate with our actual neighbors and is far from perfect.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that Mages are also power-hungry and prideful by definition, even the weaker one being able to alter reality, and add that local orders could simply form coalitions to stand against the bigger ones, something like Requiem's Circle of the Crone, or like Real Life religious federations and other similar associations formed by minor religions/companies/organizations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may sound a bit tautological to say that's not what the game is about, but... it just isn't. Awakening has well developed and well reasoned purpose behind the Orders. It not being to somebody's taste is one thing, but that's really on them. I find the statement &quot;sell me on this thing&quot; to be in rather bad faith if one is just going to dispute and deride everything people try to sell the game with. &quot;Convince me to like this game despite how terrible it is&quot; is a trap, and it's one I'm growing weary of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't intended any trap. My first assumption by creating the thread was that I was simply ignorant of what made people like the game. And to some extension, it was right. I'm actually convinced that I like most of the game, or at least can work with it without feeling it is just bad. I WILL read more, and WILL play the game now on. That said, I'm just discussing, but actually accepting regularly where I was wrong. My arguments where mostly to see if there where still something I wasn't comprehending, and most of the time there was. Yeah, on the conspiracy thing I did found an assumption where I disagree with the intent of the game on a fundamental level, but again, I'm only showcasing my opinion. I can live with that. In fact, the game is already sold to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T14:00:41-07:00","id":618053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612606#post612606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Awakening</b> is game of nWoD lines and as such is made to be very customizable. You can easily run a game when in local area the Nameless Orders ( minor, local magical societies ) are more prominent and Pentacle and Seers are nowhere near here, even after those two and a half thousand years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll do something like that, and thanks for the references.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>poindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So all we know is:<br /> <br /> FC &gt; Seers = (SL + AA || SL + Mysterium || AA + Mysterium) &gt; SL || Mysterium || AA &gt; GotV<br /> <br /> With all the Nameless combined being either slightly larger than, equal to, or smaller than the GotV, but definitely smaller than the Mysterium, SL, or AA. The exact numbers between the SL, Mysterium, and AA are unknown, and the number of Free Council could be significantly greater than the total Diamond mages (unlikely), equal to, to probably no lower than 2/3 the numbers of the complete Diamond.<br /> <br /> That's <i>very</i> open.</div> </div> </div> </div>But still stingy on the Nameless Orders. I'll see how their participation on FC or other Orders actually work, tough.<br /> <br /> Hey, those numbers actually tackled the last problem, the numbers of the Seers! Thank you very much you all, and I hope this thread helps at least one or two other persons to see the value of the game past initial prejudice from the 1st core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T14:10:28-07:00","id":618065,"title":"","content":"According to <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/new-order/\" target=\"_blank\">THIS DEVBLOG</a> about the Orders:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage has always strained at the very early nWoD\u2019s design principle of limiting the action to a single city (it makes no sense when 1/10th of starting characters can teleport.) and the Orders are global networks while simultaneously being local hierarchies that don\u2019t answer to a central authority, except for the Seers. On the other side, the structures of the Orders described in the Order books describe factions with a <i>lot</i> of members \u2013 so many that if you sit down and try to figure out how many mages there should be in a single city according to all six books put together, you rapidly go over a hundred. So, as we\u2019ve spoiled elsewhere, a single Order Caucus (for example a Guardian Epopt, all her Cultors, and the Labyrinths they\u2019re running) now covers more than one Consilium. Even then, the \u201cGuardians of the Veil\u201d is made up of every one of those Caucuses, who are all independent of one another, and have the backing of ex-Guardian archmasters. Rather than explain that the Orders are Tier 2-3 subsets of Tier 3-4 networks, we\u2019re not worrying about it. Which is why the word \u201cTier\u201d does not appear in second edition. Mages visiting foreign Caucuses are like police officers out of jurisdiction \u2013 they aren\u2019t part of the local politics, and the culture will have differences to what they\u2019re used to, but they know the job.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T14:12:25-07:00","id":618068,"title":"","content":"And if you're interested in the Nameless Orders, Dave also mentions them<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wrote the Nameless Order section of <b>Left Hand Path</b>. I have nothing against apostate characters. Compared to the line so far, we\u2019re going to see a lot more orderless mages and minor Nameless Orders (the term in Mage for an \u201cOrder\u201d that\u2019s a strictly local concern rather than being one of the six global Orders.) We\u2019ll also see a lot more advantages to being <i>in</i> a proper Order \u2013 in a standard game, everyone will have these advantages, but if you choose to play an underdog you\u2019ll understand <i>why</i> they\u2019re an underdog, \u201cgame balance\u201d be damned. Thousands of years\u2019 worth of accumulated knowledge, grimoires, rotes, Legacies, artifacts, Imbued items, and secrets are held by the Orders, if you know where to look and have the Status to get it. Each Order teaches rote mudras, provides resources where it can, trains new mages, and has proprietary Merits available to members. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T16:39:22-07:00","id":618208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=618038#post618038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a bad concept by itself. But given the nWoD tone, I think &quot;Global Conspiracy&quot; shouldn't be a core concept. Period. The nWoD was from he beginning about local mystery. In Mage, focus on local orders based on local culture would be much more interesting, the Global Conspiracy being an optional side approach (as it is everywhere else).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think I agree with this. Like Dave B, I think the game was trying to go global despite itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=618038#post618038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Humans are also insular creatures and rarely care so much for people they don't have any proximal contact. Most people barely cooperate with coworkers in such level.<br /> 2) Continual growth in transport and communication systems also improved our ability to do so without magic, and tough there are considerable advances in our ability to coordinate work, and a lot of people do this with friends far away, it came at the cost of our ability to cooperate with our actual neighbors and is far from perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think I agree with either of those. Mostly the first one. Humans naturally seek out other humans for the most part. We're biologically wired to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T16:44:15-07:00","id":618211,"title":"","content":"Monkeyspheres. Humans are driven to seek out connections, but past a certain point we can't really handle the data traffic. So you end up with us all living in big cities where nobody knows anyone's name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T17:05:23-07:00","id":618229,"title":"","content":"I don't find it accurate to describe Orders as global <u>conspiracies</u>, because to me that conjures the image of a super secret board meeting of white men who meet occasionally in some underground bunker or executive room or similar to vaguely allude to their agenda and make sinister plans for every part of the globe. The Diamond Orders are structured more like world wide religions, in which various &quot;local&quot; hierarchies (quotes because, given what they need to make caucuses functional, they'll collect over whatever area they need to in order to have enough mages) that maintain communication with each other and occasionally hold international conferences to discuss collective issues. As I recall, the Free Council is being played up as more focused on the Assembly than any collective organisation, although many will take advantage of those conferences in order to gather information and network and occasionally coordinate big maneuvers. The Seers of the Throne try to take that global conspiracy form (at least donning the trappings of it) but the command hierarchies are convoluted, distributed, and multi-layered (like how basically any Seer might receive direct orders from the Exarchs, or at least think they have). The Ministers are almost a deconstruction of the typical Illuminati council, given that they're literally incoherent and their attendents need to try and interpret their pronouncements and translate them into working policies by feel. In short, the Orders exist globally, but you're not playing the ground level soldier in some distant scheme and the actual issues in your locality and Mysteries of your residence are at the forefront of most minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T17:33:34-07:00","id":618242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't think I agree with this. Like Dave B, I think the game was trying to go global despite itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. Thing here is just my personal opinion. Understood the devs decided for a game with more focus on global conspiracy. I will just turn it down for most of my games. Isn't a bad concept by itself, just thought it could not be the &quot;default&quot; (from the use of Orders perspective, as MCN said, the game have other avenues of play).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't think I agree with either of those. Mostly the first one. Humans naturally seek out other humans for the most part. We're biologically wired to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>So tell me why we're not a great single civilization based on harmony. Human interaction is far more complex than that. Of course, I was simplifying things, but with every variable in place it is very unlikely to have such a global conspiracy really running, given all internal inconsistency that are bound to appear.<br /> <br /> But I don't think we should further this. We disagree, and it won't even make a great difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't find it accurate to describe Orders as global <u>conspiracies</u>, because to me that conjures the image of a super secret board meeting of white men who meet occasionally in some underground bunker or executive room or similar to vaguely allude to their agenda and make sinister plans for every part of the globe. The Diamond Orders are structured more like world wide religions, in which various &quot;local&quot; hierarchies (quotes because, given what they need to make caucuses functional, they'll collect over whatever area they need to in order to have enough mages) that maintain communication with each other and occasionally hold international conferences to discuss collective issues. As I recall, the Free Council is being played up as more focused on the Assembly than any collective organisation, although many will take advantage of those conferences in order to gather information and network and occasionally coordinate big maneuvers. The Seers of the Throne try to take that global conspiracy form (at least donning the trappings of it) but the command hierarchies are convoluted, distributed, and multi-layered (like how basically any Seer might receive direct orders from the Exarchs, or at least think they have). The Ministers are almost a deconstruction of the typical Illuminati council, given that they're literally incoherent and their attendents need to try and interpret their pronouncements and translate them into working policies by feel. In short, the Orders exist globally, but you're not playing the ground level soldier in some distant scheme and the actual issues in your locality and Mysteries of your residence are at the forefront of most minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe <u>institutions</u> is a better word, and this understanding is more aligned with my thoughts, but it givens credence to the idea that they don't have such awesome resources, since they don't have the central administrative infrastructure needed for such, and local orders can be as old and locally cohesive as the Diamond or the Seers. It kind of undermines the theme of global conspiracy on the game, what is to my liking, but consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T17:34:28-07:00","id":618243,"title":"","content":"Except that ... ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Orders are occult conspiracies, embedded within and working alongside Sleeper mystery cults, religions, academia, and politics. Usually, character groups for </span></span></span><b>World of Darkness</b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> games are only known by the participants. The Orders are a bit more visible than that, such that Sleepers digging into the links between occult groups will start to see that something\u2019s there. They are to Sleeper Mystery Cults as those cults are to regular people. Many Sleepers work for the Orders without ever knowing it \u2013 or work for more than one!</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T19:26:51-07:00","id":618317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=618243#post618243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that ... ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That still doesn't rule out that Orders are at the same time local conspiracies and global institutions, especially as these cults, religions, academia and politics are often local. The conspiracies don't have to stretch globally.<br /> <br /> @montparnas, about local vs global Orders: When trying to understand the orders as global institutions, you should not forget that the Diamond Orders have been trying to incorporate the Nameless Orders they ran into for hundreds, if not thousands of years (depending on the Order). Of course, this did not always work because of philosophical or practical differences, but it worked in a lot of cases because of the relatively reasonable philosophies (the foundations were already laid by mages of different Eurasian cultures comparing notes around 320 BC, in the end merging their Orders) and the metaphysical backing of the Diamond Orders. Most of the remaining Orders remained Nameless, until the Council of Free Assemblies was formed around 1900 as a way for most Nameless Orders to band together with the Diamond against the Seers. I guess most local Orders as you call them (but also less local Nameless Orders), would have become part of the Council of Free Assemblies, unless their philosophies clashed with theirs. In that case, the Orders would have stayed Nameless. Whether these Nameless Orders take place in Consilia probably depends on the Nameless Order. If they are prominent in a region, they could even have power structures different from Consilia and Assemblies.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Because of this, if you don't want to change the setting, but still give Nameless Orders a prominent place in your chronicle, you should think of reasons for these Nameless Orders to exist separately from both the Diamond Orders and the Council of Free Assemblies. If it would be possible to align their interests, becoming part of on of the global Orders has many benefits, and the Pentacle would certainly have tried to either recruit, reform or even destroy these Nameless in the past, depending on their philosophies. As Nameless Orders are relatively less powerful, the reason and way they resisted assimilation will be an important part of your setting, and possibly also a source of plot hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":".  Cleaning up my argument, and adding a second part. 08-06-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T05:42:00-07:00","id":618697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=618242#post618242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it givens credence to the idea that they don't have such awesome resources, since they don't have the central administrative infrastructure needed for such</div> </div> </div> </div>I warrant that communication and cooperation can be quite sufficient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">local orders can be as old and locally cohesive as the Diamond or the Seers</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be, but it would be important to note that there should still be a significantly different feel to something that has remained provincial and something that has spread far.<br /> <br /> There's also the significant detail of how the Orders draw upon and transmit a diverse collection of ideas and influences, which makes the whole stronger. A mage in New York can be focused primarily on the personalities and Mysteries within New York, but their ideas can come from all over the world, and that's something that a Nameless Order in New York will have less of.<br /> <br /> It's the kind of thing that one can see in To The Strongest, the idea that the meeting of those cultures allowed mages to form more sophisticated ideas about how their powers worked, something that is supposed to be substantial (even if the substance is largely outside the resolution of the mechanics).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T22:54:40-07:00","id":699513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612434#post612434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I just went back and re-read all the Seer stuff in the core, so maybe I can help you a bit more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not confirmed at all. It's just a theory held by the Atlantean orthodoxy. Same as the theory that the Watchtowers are the work of the Oracles and that the Oracles are Atlantean princes. All unconfirmed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not how Seers recruit. It's how they send marching orders.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, they seem to work together as well as the Orders do, but I guess that's just my interpretation. If anything, they seem like a very good pyramid scheme. Sure, they might interfere with each other in the lofty ideals, stuff like interpreting the grand goals of the Exarchs, but on the ground they do at least agree on opposing the Orders.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This one's easy, they have all the money and the creature comforts. Not hard to see why they'd have an easy time recruiting. From what I've gathered, they are bigger than any individual Order, but not bigger than any two, but that could also be my interpretation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ochemata are servants of the Exarchs (or any ascended being, really) sent directly to the Fallen World. They weren't in the core, sorry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not exactly the impression I got. It could just be me, but I thought that the Seers were bigger than any one of the Pentacle, but not bigger than two combined. I did get the impression that they were better than the rest at entrenching themselves in government bodies, so perhaps they have greater reach than any of the Orders.<br /> <br /> All the population talk is kind of moot, though, because every Storyteller controls the exact population of mages as they see fit. No one at White Wolf is making any charts as to the exact population of mages because that's left of to the ST at each individual table. The numbers of mages in your setting should serve YOUR story, not the other way around. There isn't some grand unified canon that you MUST adhere to in your story. If you wanted, you don't have to have a Seer presence at all, or perhaps in your city they might outnumber the Pentacle ridiculously to where it's like Neo and Trinity against a bunch of Agents all the time. It's up to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What do you mean by minor orders? Because there are such things as smaller orders that aren't the Pentacle. The Pentacle generally calls them Nameless Orders and they are a thing, but they don't have the same kind of support or magical might that the actual Orders have (rotes, artifacts, Merits like Masques or Adamantine Hand) because well ... that's just a conceit of the setting. Rather than being about local Magical Traditions (which are still a thing) it is about globe spanning conspiracies, a term which applies to the Pentacle and the Throne.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify Dave said all together the Seers are larger than the two midlevel Diamond orders with the FC being larger than that. IE the Diamond/FC have the numbers but the Seers have the money, toys, and perks to offset the fact that they DON'T have the raw numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T00:10:02-07:00","id":975404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=612155#post612155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to sum up my issues with Seers before:<br /> 1- Exarchs, the once-mage gods;<br /> 2- Recruitment through The Dream Quest of Unknown Kadath;<br /> 3- Traitorous backstabbers to the point of inneficience;<br /> 4- Sheer numbers.<br /> <br /> <br /> By what I had saw in the 1st core that was their only recruiting process, and nothing in the dev blogs I read until now seemed to change that. But if you say so, one problem less, three remain.<br /> <br /> <br /> It does make sense, tough I have no idea what an &quot;ochemata&quot; is. If it was in the core, I don't remember. Just two remain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here I will hold back a little, sorry. I do know there are plenty of hellish places to work where money never stop to come. But there ARE limits for it to be feasible. Your company still offered two protections: for the employees, that the money would actualy come most of the time, instead of taken away by corrupt colleagues or superiors. And to the superiors, that they wouldn't have to fear retaliation. And probably they didn't suffered so much from <u>their</u> superiors, so climbing the corporative ladder probably granted some respite. The Seers doesn't seem to offer any of those, and in fact be fractured enough to not even work like a company, but like a lot of them in open war against one another. That's where it becomes extremely innefective. So this problem remains to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yet a huge amount of them. I wouldn't mind so much as I do now if they where only the biggest order. But to say they're bigger than the four most traditional orders united!? Even when those orders seemed a bunch of nutjobs to me, it was still a huge number. And the Free Council being even bigger doesn't help things. To me the major power should be the regional minor orders with roots on local culture. The problem, so, remains.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, first that there IS a limit on the temptation power of that combination, both in game and IRL. Don't forget that the people they are trying to recruit are overpowered Mages themselves, you all seem to forget that when it comes to the Seers. Those &quot;exploited employees&quot; are powerful and full of potential in their own right, prone to Hubris, and so with no reason to NOT refuse all that out of simple mundane pride. There are people like this IRL, and the game assumes right from the start that Mages are like that, with no reason not to be.<br /> <br /> And second, seriously, for more that combination seems tempting, if they don't seem to have the means to make it workable, either they are very unlikely to actualy have that combination to begin with, or they will simply lose it to a more efficient group. The Guardians of the Veil seems much more competent han the Seers in this regard.<br /> <br /> Out of four, two issues where taken, two remain. That's just me keeping personal tabs, though, I will read further explanations, and I do feel the Seers at least usable now. The backstabbing part needs to be toned down a bit, without loss to the feeling of abuse and claustrophobia from within. That's manageable. The size is still to great, but without the other problems it is less of one. And also one I can correct without so much trouble as the two better addressed would have.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bTry again and this time make it at least something marginally convincing to someone that isn't bought by sticks and asks that the carrots better be way better then give me your soul to command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T05:06:18-07:00","id":975474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=975404#post975404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bTry again and this time make it at least something marginally convincing to someone that isn't bought by sticks and asks that the carrots better be way better then give me your soul to command.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize he's saying he has problems with the Seer setup, don't you? He's not trying to recruit, he's saying that he doesn't understand how their recruiting works. Bit of a misdirected reaction on your part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T06:31:31-07:00","id":975489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=975474#post975474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You realize he's saying he has problems with the Seer setup, don't you? He's not trying to recruit, he's saying that he doesn't understand how their recruiting works. Bit of a misdirected reaction on your part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That and asking for someone to respond to post they wrote a year ago is kinda pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T19:52:57-07:00","id":985900,"title":"","content":"Curiously I do read this thread from time to time. For the last year and a month, or so, my work had taken most of my time. I hope to lessen this by now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar304_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"304\" data-vbnamecard=\"304\">Penta</a> I do want, in the end, to change the setting, at least a little. My take on the whole CoD is that the groups (Covenants, Tribes, Orders) given work better as examples, not an exhaustive list. Even if &quot;only&quot; an exhaustive list of globaly relevant ones.<br /> <br /> By now, I think I did understood the argument of the setting &quot;as is&quot;, it just don't convince me. To be precise, I see no reason whatsoever for the &quot;Nameless Orders&quot; (that would hardly be nameless by their own standards) to be less resourcefull in their turf. Simple contact isn't enough to explain such distinction. There are no reason to think that several groups exchanging research notes for centuries are bound to become only one group just because they have some common philosophies. Take as a simple example the city of Istanbul: since its time as Constantinople it was a place where numerous sages, philosophers, scientists and highly educated priests of several religions and places, from western Cristians to chinese Taoists, could congregate to trade knowledge and thougts. The result was, for centuries, the greatest place on Earth for advancement of human knowledge, where most of modern sciences where developed to something similar to what we have today, including astronomy, physics, chemistry and mathematics. Those people do exchange knowledge and philosophies to a great degree, as they do even today in a lot of ways. And... they're still as distinct as people, philosophies and institutions as ever.<br /> <br /> Well, I'm not sure if I made myself clear, but I liked how people are presenting their takes on the setting in this thread. It, actualy, made a lot for my interest on the books and on running Mage at some opportunity, more than any particular argument (I'm not saying in any way mine are better than anyone else's).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T23:27:36-07:00","id":985967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=985900#post985900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do want, in the end, to change the setting, at least a little. My take on the whole CoD is that the groups (Covenants, Tribes, Orders) given work better as examples, not an exhaustive list. Even if &quot;only&quot; an exhaustive list of globaly relevant ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is how things always worked in Mage. Even if, for example, Guardians have main doctrine all around the world, ones from New York and those from New Delhi will look totally diffrent, having their own customs and, yes, heresis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=985900#post985900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be precise, I see no reason whatsoever for the &quot;Nameless Orders&quot; (that would hardly be nameless by their own standards) to be less resourcefull in their turf. Simple contact isn't enough to explain such distinction. There are no reason to think that several groups exchanging research notes for centuries are bound to become only one group just because they have some common philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your problem is that your hinged on idea 'Orders look the same everywhere' - which is not true, if you look in to Order books. Orders <i>where</i> Nameless Orders themselves before ( called Darshanas ) that went in to global alliance some time after Alexander the Great. Now previous Nameless Orders that formed those are <i>Factions</i> in greater Orders. Just see any Pentacle Order book ( beside Free Council ) and you see that every Diamond Order is just collection of different philosophies and occult traditions, i.e. previous Nameless Orders. They just forget they are 'Nameless' still, just too sound more bigger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=985900#post985900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take as a simple example the city of Istanbul: since its time as Constantinople it was a place where numerous sages, philosophers, scientists and highly educated priests of several religions and places, from western Cristians to chinese Taoists, could congregate to trade knowledge and thougts. The result was, for centuries, the greatest place on Earth for advancement of human knowledge, where most of modern sciences where developed to something similar to what we have today, including astronomy, physics, chemistry and mathematics. Those people do exchange knowledge and philosophies to a great degree, as they do even today in a lot of ways. And... they're still as distinct as people, philosophies and institutions as ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is how Pentacle and Diamond Orders work now - just read Order books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T03:54:59-07:00","id":986030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=985900#post985900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curiously I do read this thread from time to time. For the last year and a month, or so, my work had taken most of my time. I hope to lessen this by now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar304_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"304\" data-vbnamecard=\"304\">Penta</a> I do want, in the end, to change the setting, at least a little. My take on the whole CoD is that the groups (Covenants, Tribes, Orders) given work better as examples, not an exhaustive list. Even if &quot;only&quot; an exhaustive list of globaly relevant ones.<br /> <br /> By now, I think I did understood the argument of the setting &quot;as is&quot;, it just don't convince me. To be precise, I see no reason whatsoever for the &quot;Nameless Orders&quot; (that would hardly be nameless by their own standards) to be less resourcefull in their turf. Simple contact isn't enough to explain such distinction. There are no reason to think that several groups exchanging research notes for centuries are bound to become only one group just because they have some common philosophies. Take as a simple example the city of Istanbul: since its time as Constantinople it was a place where numerous sages, philosophers, scientists and highly educated priests of several religions and places, from western Cristians to chinese Taoists, could congregate to trade knowledge and thougts. The result was, for centuries, the greatest place on Earth for advancement of human knowledge, where most of modern sciences where developed to something similar to what we have today, including astronomy, physics, chemistry and mathematics. Those people do exchange knowledge and philosophies to a great degree, as they do even today in a lot of ways. And... they're still as distinct as people, philosophies and institutions as ever.<br /> <br /> Well, I'm not sure if I made myself clear, but I liked how people are presenting their takes on the setting in this thread. It, actualy, made a lot for my interest on the books and on running Mage at some opportunity, more than any particular argument (I'm not saying in any way mine are better than anyone else's).</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why dont you use the nameless orders merits for free? They give the exact same bonus as the main orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:13:18-07:00","id":986173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is how things always worked in Mage. Even if, for example, Guardians have main doctrine all around the world, ones from New York and those from New Delhi will look totally diffrent, having their own customs and, yes, heresis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also how it worked with any of those. And yet, if sometimes you find a city where the Lancea et Sanctum works in quite a distinct and heretical way, in others you can have a covenant as complete as those in the book, but completely unrelated. As Tokyo City in the very 2nd Edition Requiem Core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your problem is that your hinged on idea 'Orders look the same everywhere' - which is not true, if you look in to Order books. Orders <i>where</i> Nameless Orders themselves before ( called Darshanas ) that went in to global alliance some time after Alexander the Great. Now previous Nameless Orders that formed those are<i>Factions</i> in greater Orders. Just see any Pentacle Order book ( beside Free Council ) and you see that every Diamond Order is just collection of different philosophies and occult traditions, i.e. previous Nameless Orders. They just forget they are 'Nameless' still, just too sound more bigger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nop, I quite got that already. My problem is that it isn't enough for me, just that. And that I still see no reason for Orders who didn't allied with others to be less resourcefull in their turf. That is, I can see reason for a &quot;Nameless Order&quot; to not have its influence spreading as much, but I see no reason whatsoever for such Order to not have equivalent benefits to that of the Pentacle/FC/Seers in <u>their</u> cities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is how Pentacle and Diamond Orders work now - just read Order books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it is more similar to &quot;organized&quot; religions, that are far less organized as it seems. Just read about the miriad variations of Budhism in India, China, Tibet and Japan, and at the same time, in China Budhism neared Confucionism and Thaoism a lot, to the point of a lot of people following the three at some degree, but yet they persist not being in any way under the same flag, not even there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why dont you use the nameless orders merits for free? They give the exact same bonus as the main orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably I will do. I was just arguing about the setting &quot;as is&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:16:41-07:00","id":986204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=986173#post986173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nop, I quite got that already. My problem is that it isn't enough for me, just that. And that I still see no reason for Orders who didn't allied with others to be less resourcefull in their turf. That is, I can see reason for a &quot;Nameless Order&quot; to not have its influence spreading as much, but I see no reason whatsoever for such Order to not have equivalent benefits to that of the Pentacle/FC/Seers in <u>their</u> cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you should look in to Tuscon official setting in 2E corebook. City is run by only Nameless Order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:20:10-07:00","id":986237,"title":"","content":"The book doesn't really play up conflict much, I think that's part of Mage that has always varied from the others of the Big Three, Vampire and Werewolf. In both of them, everyone's a killing machine and is expected to have killed someone at some point. In mage, while everyone has the capability to do it, it's likely to not pop up, and those who want conflict have the Arrow for it.<br /> <br /> Even the Free Council, who have among their core beliefs, 'Destroy the Followers of the Lie,' explains that only taking that to the point of wanting to actually destroy the followers of the lie is something radicals do. Most believe that peaceful cooperation with the Pentacle is the best bet for that.<br /> <br /> I was looking through the cities and came upon this, in LA. The Seers operate these cults to gain access to and influence over celebrities and people in the entertainment industry. P273, 'Rivalries between these cults and similar cults run by local Guardians of the Veil occasionally become sufficiently heated that celebrity gossip magazines periodically carry stories about animosity between wealthy and powerful people in rival &quot;spiritual organizations.&quot; Cults run by the Seers of the Throne also commonly use threats of lawsuits and similar forms of intimidation to attempt to prevent journalists or bloggers from posting any remotely negative information about them.' That's in a city that has been rife with police and governmental corruption since its inception, not to mention the racial tensions.<br /> <br /> That's not the kind of thing that's going to make someone who's come out of a Forsaken War Against the Pure or a conflict between Technocrats and Traditions think there's a lot of risks in the world of Awakening. Most of the cities depict, essentially, 'first world problems.' In Spain, the Seers are trying to get access to, basically, journals of peoples explorations. In Tuscon, they operate out of a rich suburb and 'rarely involve themselves with other mages in the city, viewing the Nameless as neither a threat to their own existences, nor a strong enough tool to help dismantle the Pentacle.'<br /> <br /> I've been sold on mage with second edition. But I think some people, like myself, will need to read between the lines and shift the focus to certain things to make the setting more palatable. Which is fine, because Chronicles is good for that. Play the Seers not as bumbling thickheaded fat-cats, but as an organized and opportunistic threat that already has all the cards and the House telling them what needs to be done. Play up the political, territorial and Obsession angles with mages so that there is conflict among them. 'The great flaw of the Awakened is hubris, the certainty that their obsessions are an end worth any means.' This is just begging for internal conflict. Each of the Orders has some sub-faction that sort of acts as a heresy and can really throw a monkey wrench in the works of PC cabals. If players are getting too flashy with their magic, paradox is the least of their problems. There exists an entire Order that might decide a mage is unworthy of having their magic and too dangerous to exist. Becoming scelesti is an option available at all times to any mage, and you don't have to be Chaotic Evil or Chaotic Stupid to take it. Souls and human sacrifice are sources of power that might make the difference between life or death for a mage and everyone they care about.<br /> <br /> These things are there, in the books. But they're not really played up in the core and most of the discussions about mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-12-2016, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:22:05-07:00","id":986432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=986237#post986237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book doesn't really play up conflict much, I think that's part of Mage that has always varied from the others of the Big Three, Vampire and Werewolf. In both of them, everyone's a killing machine and is expected to have killed someone at some point. In mage, while everyone has the capability to do it, it's likely to not pop up, and those who want conflict have the Arrow for it.<br /> <br /> Even the Free Council, who have among their core beliefs, 'Destroy the Followers of the Lie,' explains that only taking that to the point of wanting to actually destroy the followers of the lie is something radicals do. Most believe that peaceful cooperation with the Pentacle is the best bet for that.<br /> <br /> I was looking through the cities and came upon this, in LA. The Seers operate these cults to gain access to and influence over celebrities and people in the entertainment industry. P273, 'Rivalries between these cults and similar cults run by local Guardians of the Veil occasionally become sufficiently heated that celebrity gossip magazines periodically carry stories about animosity between wealthy and powerful people in rival &quot;spiritual organizations.&quot; Cults run by the Seers of the Throne also commonly use threats of lawsuits and similar forms of intimidation to attempt to prevent journalists or bloggers from posting any remotely negative information about them.' That's in a city that has been rife with police and governmental corruption since its inception, not to mention the racial tensions.<br /> <br /> That's not the kind of thing that's going to make someone who's come out of a Forsaken War Against the Pure or a conflict between Technocrats and Traditions think there's a lot of risks in the world of Awakening. Most of the cities depict, essentially, 'first world problems.' In Spain, the Seers are trying to get access to, basically, journals of peoples explorations. In Tuscon, they operate out of a rich suburb and 'rarely involve themselves with other mages in the city, viewing the Nameless as neither a threat to their own existences, nor a strong enough tool to help dismantle the Pentacle.'<br /> <br /> I've been sold on mage with second edition. But I think some people, like myself, will need to read between the lines and shift the focus to certain things to make the setting more palatable. Which is fine, because Chronicles is good for that. Play the Seers not as bumbling thickheaded fat-cats, but as an organized and opportunistic threat that already has all the cards and the House telling them what needs to be done. Play up the political, territorial and Obsession angles with mages so that there is conflict among them. 'The great flaw of the Awakened is hubris, the certainty that their obsessions are an end worth any means.' This is just begging for internal conflict. Each of the Orders has some sub-faction that sort of acts as a heresy and can really throw a monkey wrench in the works of PC cabals. If players are getting too flashy with their magic, paradox is the least of their problems. There exists an entire Order that might decide a mage is unworthy of having their magic and too dangerous to exist. Becoming scelesti is an option available at all times to any mage, and you don't have to be Chaotic Evil or Chaotic Stupid to take it. Souls and human sacrifice are sources of power that might make the difference between life or death for a mage and everyone they care about.<br /> <br /> These things are there, in the books. But they're not really played up in the core and most of the discussions about mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like moving to more <i>personal</i> threats and problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T17:33:09-07:00","id":986489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/609622-sell-me-on-mage-the-awakening?p=986432#post986432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like moving to more <i>personal</i> threats and problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great. All the games I mentioned offer that, as do many of the situations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}